        "title": "Structural Masonry: Load Paths, Slenderness, Reinforcement, and Codes",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Structural masonry design has two modes: empirical (rule-of-thumb h/t limits, no calculation) and engineered (stress analysis per TMS 402/ACI 530). The governing standard in the US is **TMS 402** (Masonry Society / American Concrete Institute / ASCE). Modern reinforced masonry works similarly to reinforced concrete — steel takes tension, masonry takes compression."
    },
